      "data": {
        "title": "Build the Handle Primitive and One Projection Smoke Test",
        "action": "Define Port as the base endpoint primitive and Handle as its operative specialization. Define the Title-centered circular interface frame, Declaration-derived root direction and radius, Handle-to-Port edge creation, optional empty-drop actions, and action-target authority. Upgrade the Dynamic Port Expansion smoke graph so three authored section records project three Handles onto the boundary, create Wikipedia Section nodes, and connect to their receiving Ports.",
        "expectedEvidence": "The class graph visibly explains what the node accepts, which Ports are actionable Handles, what optional actions they offer, and where those endpoints project on the circle. Auto-layout arranges portals and other content inside the frame without changing endpoint directions. Runtime instances contain no unexplained synthetic side handles, redundant matching Ports, or manually authored angle, side, radius, or offset.",
        "status": "todo",
        "definitionKey": "idea-next-step",
